* rt_xmp.cal: test runtime for the X-MP mode, direct start.
*
* As rt_direct.cal, for the machine with the X-MP features (MACHINE XMP):
* the dead start loads the X-MP form of the exchange package at words 0-17.
* Monitor mode, cluster 0, instruction and data fields from word 0 to the
* end of the four million words.  A0-A7, S0-S7 and VL start as 0.
*
*          INCLUDE "rt_xmp.cal"
*          TBEGIN
*          ... the test, ending in TPASS or TFAIL n ...
*          TEND
*          ... data ...
*          END
*
* The macros are those of rt_common.cal.  A test for this runtime has the
* line "         MACHINE XMP" itself (this file's is undone by nothing, but
* the tools look for the line in the test to pick the machine).
*
         MACHINE XMP
T$IO     =       17777760
         INCLUDE "rt_common.cal"
T$P2_29  =       4000000000              ; 2**29: the base and limit fields
T$XLMAX  =       1777777                 ; the largest base or limit field
*
         ORG     0
         CON     T$ENTRY*4*T$P2_24       ; P = entry parcel; A0 = 0
         CON     0                       ; IBA = 0; A1 = 0
         CON     T$XLMAX*T$P2_29+1*T$P2_24 ; ILA; monitor mode; A2 = 0
         CON     0                       ; XA = 0, VL = 0, F = 0; A3 = 0
         CON     0                       ; DBA = 0, cluster 0; A4 = 0
         CON     T$XLMAX*T$P2_29         ; DLA; A5 = 0
         BSSZ    D'10                    ; A6, A7, S0-S7
*
         MACRO   TUSER %BA
         ENDM
*
         MACRO   TBEGIN
         ORG     T$ENTRY
         ENDM
*
         MACRO   TEND %DUMP
T$END    %DUMP
         S2      T$CDON,0
         T$DONE,0 S2
         S1      T$STAT,0
         S2      1
         S0      S1\S2
         JSN     T$EXW
         S1      0
T$EXW    T$EXIT,0 S1
T$HANG   J       T$HANG
         ENDM
